Harold sleeps for 10 hours a night. He works 2 hours less than he sleeps, so he works 10 - 2 = 8 hours a day. He walks his dog for 1 hour each day. Total time Harold spends on sleeping, working, and dog-walking is: 10 hours (sleeping) + 8 hours (working) + 1 hour (dog-walking) = 19 hours. There are 24 hours in a day. So, Harold's free time is: 24 hours (day) - 19 hours (sleeping, working, dog-walking) = 5 hours.
\boxed{5}

